fix(scripts): give the scheduled backup a PATH that finds docker

The schedule installed and loaded and could not run. A launchd user agent
inherits /usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin and nothing else, and Docker Desktop is
on none of them, so the first on-demand firing wrote one line to its log:

    backup-ledger: no container named innsegl-postgres -- is the stack up?

A backup that cannot run is the failure scripts/backup-ledger.sh's own header
is about, arriving through the door built to fix backups that never run. It
installed cleanly, `launchctl list` showed it, and `status` read the command
back out of the unit. Everything said yes except the job.

The directories of `docker` and `git` are now resolved at install time and
written into the unit, as EnvironmentVariables on launchd and Environment= on
systemd. Resolved rather than hardcoded, because a shipped file may not name a
directory on the operator's machine and because Docker Desktop, Colima,
Homebrew and a Linux package manager each put it somewhere different. `status`
prints the path too, so a job that cannot find its tools is visible without
opening the unit file.

Measured after the fix. The agent fired on demand, with nothing else running
it, and wrote a dump and its verification report to the backup directory:
630 events at positions 1 to 630, adjudicated against the sealed segments by
runbooks/verify-rebuilt-index.sh, ending "rebuilt index vs sealed segments:
OK".

Driven by OPS-035, extended to require the installed unit to name the
directory docker is actually in, and watched failing first against the unit
that had none.

